CheapNeuroSim is a comprehensive C# neurochemistry simulation namespace that models artificial brains with realistic neural dynamics, emotions, memory, social behavior, and genetic inheritance.

Core Architecture
Neural System
Brain.cs - The main neural simulation engine (sealed class)

Manages neuron activations, synaptic propagation, and learning
Uses 3 activation states: _activation (current), _nextActivation (buffer), _lastActivation (previous)
Implements Hebbian learning with plasticity scaling
Tracks ~400 lines of core simulation logic
BrainGenome.cs - Genetic blueprint for brains

Contains immutable brain architecture (neurons & synapses)
Supports genetic mutations with customizable settings
Pre-wires innate survival circuits (eat, flee, rest, explore, signal)
Generates seeded random genomes
NeuronGene.cs & SynapseGene.cs - Individual neural components

Neurons: bias, excitability, leak, action target/weight
Synapses: source/destination, weight, plasticity
Input/Output Channels (BrainChannels.cs)
Standardized sensor/action channels:

Sensors: Hunger, Threat, Pain, Social, Novelty, Energy
Actions: Eat, Flee, Rest, Explore, Bond, Signal, and others
Neurochemical System
NeurochemicalState.cs - 6 key neurotransmitters that modulate behavior:

Dopamine (0-1) - Reward, motivation, novelty drive
Serotonin (0-1) - Mood stability, calm
Norepinephrine (0-1) - Alertness, arousal
Cortisol (0-1) - Stress response
Oxytocin (0-1) - Bonding, affiliation
Acetylcholine (0-1) - Learning, attention
Dynamics respond to inputs (hunger, threat, pain, social, novelty, energy), rewards, and brain temperament.

Emotional System
EmotionKind.cs - 9 emotion types:

Calm, Afraid, Curious, Lonely, Craving, Affectionate, Angry, Exhausted, Hurt
EmotionState.cs - Tracks individual emotional values (0-1) plus a "Primary" dominant emotion determined by neurochemical/need states.

Personality & Temperament
PersonalityStyle.cs - 7 personality archetypes:

Balanced, Timid, Impulsive, Gregarious, Obsessive, Suspicious, Dutiful
TemperamentProfile.cs - Heritable traits:

Novelty Seeking, Harm Avoidance, Reward Dependence, Sociability, Learning Rate, Impulse Control
PersonalityExpression.cs - Derives current personality from state (temperament + addiction + trauma + needs).

Memory Systems
EpisodicMemoryState.cs - Records memories with:

Emotional valence (reward/threat)
Social context (group associations)
Novelty/salience tracking
Consolidation into culture beliefs during offline sleep
MemoryTrace.cs - Individual memory entries MemoryDebugSnapshot.cs - Debug snapshots of memory state

Needs & Motivation
NeedsState.cs - 5 core needs (0-1):

Energy, Nutrition, Integrity (health), Healing, Social
NeedsProfile.cs - Genetic predisposition for need sensitivity

Addiction System
AddictionState.cs - Tracks:

Craving intensity
Withdrawal symptoms
Tolerance buildup
Sensitization to triggers
AddictiveStimulus.cs - Describes dopamine/reward stimuli that can cause addiction.

Attention & Goals
AttentionState.cs - Filters sensory input with:

Threat/Pain levels
Novelty salience
Dominant focus for sensor gain modulation
GoalState.cs - Tracks:

Active goals and their intensity
Goal satisfaction/pursuit state
GoalKind.cs - Goal types (e.g., survive, reproduce, bond, explore).

Social & Cultural Behavior
SocialBiasState.cs - In-group/out-group bias:

Learns group affiliations & threat associations
Evaluates attitude (affiliation vs. threat) toward groups
Modulates oxytocin/cortisol based on group membership
SocialIdentity.cs - Individual/group identity markers SocialSignal.cs - Emotional contagion (affiliation, stress, valence) CultureState.cs - Cultural beliefs and memes shared within groups CulturalMeme.cs - Beliefs that spread with mutation & virulence ReputationState.cs - Tracks reputation with specific individuals

Development & Trauma
DevelopmentState.cs - Life stages (Newborn → Adult) affecting:

Culture uptake multiplier
Impulse control development
Plasticity changes
DevelopmentStage.cs - Enum of development phases

TraumaState.cs - PTSD-like responses:

Hypervigilance
Trigger load
Recovery mechanisms
Utilities & Debug
BrainType.cs - Architecture template defining:

Neuron/synapse/sensor/action counts
Chemical profile
Baseline plasticity
BrainInput/BrainOutput.cs - I/O vectors

BrainDebugSnapshot.cs - Captures complete brain state for debugging BrainRuntimeState.cs - Saves/restores runtime simulation state

SynapseDebugStats.cs - Tracks synapse weight statistics (min/max/average)

MathUtil.cs - Utility functions (clamping, approach, tanh, etc.)

StableRandom.cs - Seeded random generator for reproducible mutations

MutationSettings.cs - Controls mutation rates & intensity

Integration
The system interconnects through the Brain.Tick() method:

Input injection → sensor gains modulated by attention
Synapse propagation → weighted neuron activations
Neurochemical update → responds to inputs/rewards
Emotion evaluation → driven by chemicals + needs + trauma
Action projection → neuron outputs scaled by dopamine/serotonin
Learning → Hebbian + reward + stress modulation
Memory recording → important events stored episodically
